So the problem is tug, with the highest observed frequency in the construction. It returns NaN with precbitsexponent=3, 4, and 5 (with precbitsexponent=4, the script needed maybe 7 minutes or so and the R instance required about 4.2 GB of RAM). I am currently looking into where the error comes from - right now, I can see that the NaN at least originates in hypergeom.mpfr ,but it may take me a while to get to the bottom of this so my recommendation for now would be to just use LLR as the measure of collocational strength because its computation won't collapse and it's so highly correlated with FYE that the results are most of the time not different enough.

